# rfipconfig-fe — Shipwright Build (frontend)

Frontend counterpart of `rfipconfig-be-s2i-build`. Same namespace (`openshift-builds`), same `pipeline` ServiceAccount, same `s2i` ClusterBuildStrategy, same `pipeline-push-secret`. No new RBAC needed — `rb-pipeline-image-builder` already covers pushes to the internal registry.

---

## 1. BE vs FE — what actually differs

The two Builds share the same skeleton. Only these fields carry different values:

| Field (path in Build spec) | Backend (`rfipconfig-be.yaml`) | Frontend (`rfipconfig-fe.yaml`) | Why it differs |
|---|---|---|---|
| `metadata.name` | `rfipconfig-be-s2i-build` | `rfipconfig-fe-s2i-build` | Separate Build resource per app |
| `spec.env` → app vars | `DOTNET_PACK=true`, `DOTNET_STARTUP_PROJECT=Rfipconfig.Api.csproj` | .NET vars removed; Node-style vars (e.g. `NPM_RUN`, `NODE_ENV`) as needed | BE is .NET S2I, FE is a different runtime — builder-specific env |
| `spec.env` → `PORT` | `5000` | `CHANGE_ME` (e.g. `8080`) | FE listens on its own port |
| `spec.source.git.url` | `git@hlgithub.hobbylobby.corp:Warehouse/rfipconfig.git` | `CHANGE_ME` — same repo or a separate FE repo | Depends on repo layout |
| `spec.source.git.cloneSecret` | `github-repo-ssh-key-rfipconfig-be` | `github-repo-ssh-key-rfipconfig-fe` (or reuse the BE secret) | Separate deploy key only if FE is a separate repo |
| `spec.source.git.revision` | `master` | `CHANGE_ME` | FE repo/branch may differ |
| `spec.source.contextDir` | `Rfipconfig.Api` | `CHANGE_ME` (e.g. `Rfipconfig.Web`) | Different source directory |
| `paramValues` → `builder-image` | `quay.hobbylobby.corp/hl-images/hl-dotnet:60-rhel9-latest` | `CHANGE_ME` (e.g. an hl Node.js/nginx S2I builder from Quay) | Runtime-specific builder |
| `spec.output.image` | `.../openshift-builds/rfipconfig-be:latest` | `.../openshift-builds/rfipconfig-fe:<tag>` | Separate image repository per app |

**Identical in both (do not edit):**

| Field | Shared value | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| `metadata.namespace` | `openshift-builds` | Verified existing namespace with working RBAC |
| `spec.env` → `SSL_CERT_FILE` | `/etc/pki/ca-trust/extracted/trust-manager/ca-certs.pem` | Quay internal-CA trust workaround |
| `spec.source.git.depth` | `1` | Shallow clone |
| `spec.strategy` | `s2i` / `ClusterBuildStrategy` | Shared strategy (CA volume + `registries-search` already configured) |
| `spec.output.pushSecret` | `pipeline-push-secret` | Existing `dockerconfigjson` secret |
| BuildRun `spec.serviceAccount` | `pipeline` | Holds `system:image-builder` via `rb-pipeline-image-builder` |

