## 2. File-by-file, line-by-line edit guide

### `rfipconfig-fe.yaml` — 7 required edits

| # | Line | Field | What to enter | Example |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **26–27** | `env` → `PORT` | Port the FE app listens on | `"8080"` |
| 2 | **17–23** | `env` (commented block) | Uncomment/add runtime env vars the FE builder needs; delete the block if none | `NPM_RUN=build`, `NODE_ENV=production` |
| 3 | **35** | `source.git.url` | FE repo SSH URL. Same repo as BE → copy the BE URL and only change `contextDir` | `git@hlgithub.hobbylobby.corp:Warehouse/rfipconfig.git` |
| 4 | **38** | `source.git.cloneSecret` | Secret name for the deploy key. Same repo as BE → change to `github-repo-ssh-key-rfipconfig-be` and skip `secret-fe-ssh-key.yaml` | `github-repo-ssh-key-rfipconfig-fe` |
| 5 | **41** | `source.git.revision` | Branch to build | `master` |
| 6 | **43** | `source.contextDir` | Directory of FE source inside the repo | `Rfipconfig.Web` |
| 7 | **50–51** | `paramValues` → `builder-image` | S2I builder image from `quay.hobbylobby.corp` (not the old `hl-images` internal-registry namespace) | `quay.hobbylobby.corp/hl-images/hl-nodejs:18-rhel9-latest` |
| 8 | **59** | `output.image` (tag only) | Replace `:CHANGE_ME` with the tag; keep the path | `:latest` |

Optional: **lines 54–55** — uncomment `storage-driver: overlay` only if you want to override the strategy default (`vfs`).

Keep unchanged: line 12 (`name`), line 13 (`namespace`), lines 28–29 (`SSL_CERT_FILE`), lines 45–47 (`strategy`), line 61 (`pushSecret`).

### `buildrun-rfipconfig-fe.yaml` — no edits required

| Line | Field | Note |
|---|---|---|
| 12 | `generateName: rfipconfig-fe-s2i-build-` | Each run gets a unique suffix → must use `oc create`, **not** `oc apply` |
| 16 | `build.name` | Must match `metadata.name` in `rfipconfig-fe.yaml` line 12 — only change if you rename the Build |
| 18 | `serviceAccount: pipeline` | Keep — existing SA with image-builder RBAC |

### `secret-fe-ssh-key.yaml` — conditional (only for a separate FE deploy key)

| Line | Field | What to do |
|---|---|---|
| 12 | `--from-file=ssh-privatekey=CHANGE_ME` | Preferred path: run the `oc create secret` command in the header with your key file path — the key never touches Git |
| 24 | `stringData.ssh-privatekey` | Only if applying the manifest directly: paste the private key at apply time; never commit it |

Skip this file entirely if the FE lives in the same repo as the BE (edit #4 above → reuse the BE secret).

