## 3. Apply order

```bash
# 1. (only if a separate deploy key is needed)
oc create secret generic github-repo-ssh-key-rfipconfig-fe \
  --namespace openshift-builds \
  --type=kubernetes.io/ssh-auth \
  --from-file=ssh-privatekey=<path-to-key>

# 2. Build definition
oc apply -f rfipconfig-fe.yaml

# 3. Verify (fully qualified type — plain `oc get build` resolves to legacy build.openshift.io)
oc get builds.shipwright.io -n openshift-builds

# 4. Trigger a run (create, not apply — generateName)
oc create -f buildrun-rfipconfig-fe.yaml

# 5. Watch
oc get buildruns.shipwright.io -n openshift-builds -w
```

## 4. Verification notes

- Check status via CLI (`oc get buildruns.shipwright.io`), not the console — the console plugin BuildRun detail page can crash with React error #310 (OCPBUGS-84214) even when the build succeeds.
- Clone step auth failure → confirm secret type is `kubernetes.io/ssh-auth` and the deploy key is registered on the FE repo.
- Quay pull TLS failure → confirm the `trust-manager-ca` ConfigMap (`hobbylobby.corp`) contains the CA; `SSL_CERT_FILE` is already set and the strategy mounts the CA at `/etc/pki/ca-trust/extracted/trust-manager`.
